# URLs that a human can visit but the CI linkchecker (lychee) cannot.
# The pages exist; their servers block automated clients with 403 or
# quietly time them out.  Verified in-browser on 2026-08-03.
#
# One regex per line, anchored implicitly.  If any entry ever hides a
# genuinely-dead link, remove it and let CI fail.

# ISO standards catalogue: 403 to non-browser user-agents.
^https?://(www\.)?iso\.org/

# MDPI journals: 403 to bots.
^https?://(dx\.)?doi\.org/10\.3390/

# cppreference.com: 403 to bots.
^https?://en\.cppreference\.com/

# The Word Factory: connection times out to bots.
^https?://(www\.)?thewordfactory\.com/

# Stack Exchange sites: 403 to bots.
^https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)?stackexchange\.com/
^https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)?stackoverflow\.com/
